<Base title="Privacy and Browser Storage" description="How FreeJapaneseAcademy stores learning progress on your device and how to export or delete it." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Privacy',href:'/privacy/'}]}>
  <article class="prose-page"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR DATA</span><h1>Privacy & browser storage</h1><p>Last updated: November 2, 2026</p><h2>Progress on your device</h2><p>FreeJapaneseAcademy currently has no student account system. If you mark a lesson complete, bookmark a lesson, or take a demonstration quiz, that information is stored in your browser using IndexedDB. It is not automatically uploaded to a learning account or synchronized across devices.</p><h2>What's stored</h2><p>Your browser may store lesson identifiers and completion times, quiz results and timestamps, bookmarks, and settings you choose. You can view, export, import, or erase this data from the <a class="text-link" href="/dashboard/">dashboard</a>.</p><h2>Backups and clearing browser data</h2><p>Browser storage can be erased when you clear site data, use certain private browsing modes, or remove your browser profile. Export a JSON backup if you want to keep your progress. Imported files remain on your device and are validated before they replace existing progress.</p><h2>Google AdSense and advertising</h2><p>We have added Google AdSense (publisher ID <code>pub-3399213817491318</code>) to help support free Japanese learning. A Google advertising script is included on pages of this website. Loading the script can initiate network requests to Google and disclose technical information such as your IP address, browser information, and page URL. Depending on whether advertising is enabled, where you live, and applicable consent choices, Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to show and measure advertisements. See <a class="text-link" href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information for advertising</a> for additional details.</p><p>Personalized advertising for visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK, and Switzerland requires an appropriate Google-certified consent management platform (CMP). AdSense consent messages and ad personalization preferences must be configured through the publisher's AdSense account before those features are enabled. The presence of this script does not mean that advertisements are already being displayed.</p><h2>Contact form submissions</h2><p>If you use the <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact form</a>, your name, email address, topic, and message are submitted directly to <a class="text-link" href="https://formsubmit.co/" rel="noopener noreferrer">FormSubmit</a>, an independent service that processes them to forward your enquiry to <a class="text-link" href="mailto:free-japanese-academy@protonmail.com">free-japanese-academy@protonmail.com</a>. FormSubmit may perform spam and CAPTCHA checks. It states that it retains form submissions for 30 days. These messages are not stored in our browser-side learning progress database. Please do not include sensitive personal information. You can email us directly instead of using the form.</p><h2>Hosting and technical requests</h2><p>The website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Like other websites, the hosting infrastructure processes requests needed to deliver pages. This page describes the application's browser-side learning data; it does not imply that infrastructure request logs or browser networking data do not exist. Third-party advertising is described above. Other future integrations may require additional privacy notice updates.</p><h2>Questions and updates</h2><p>This privacy explanation will be updated as new features are added. You can reach us via the <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">contact page</a>. No student account is required to study.</p></article>
</Base>
